  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 317 AM EDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nTuesday - Friday Afternoon...\n\nA shortwave and its associated surface low will move through the \neastern Great Lakes toward New England on Tuesday. A cold front \ntrailing from this feature will slide through our area pretty early \nin the day, with shower and storm chances shutting down across our \neast through the day. For now, it looks like any stronger storm \nactivity will develop east of our area, but it does appear there \nwill be a brief warm sector Tuesday morning before frontal passage. \nSo, not completely ready to rule out that we could still see a \nstrong storm or two Tuesday morning before the storm threat shuts \ndown.\n\nOur S and SW CWA will have the longest residence time ahead of \nfrontal passage and are still expected to squeeze out highs in the \nlow 90s. Given that dew points are likely to be in the mid to upper \n70s, we'll likely flirt with Heat Advisory criteria along the KY/TN \nborder and across west central KY. Medium confidence we'll need a \nheadline for Tuesday for at least some of the CWA.\n\nThe upper pattern through mid to late week will continue to feature \nNW flow aloft between the central CONUS ridge, and the closed upper \nlow meandering over New England. Overall, looks like a dry stretch \nas the upper pattern looks void of any notable features/triggers. \nTemps will be a bit cooler behind the front and will feature highs \nin the mid to upper 80s each day. Dew points will also be notably \nlower behind the front, and generally around the low 60s. This will \nlead to more pleasant nighttime lows mostly in the 60s.\n\nFriday Evening - Sunday...\n\nOur dry stretch of weather likely comes to an end as we head into the \nweekend. The upper ridge to our west will break down as a shortwave \ndigs on the northern periphery, and will likely slide into the mid \nMississippi or Tennessee River Valley for the weekend. Shower and \nstorm chances will be increasing through this time. A bit concerned \nthis could bring a localized flooding threat as it will be a \nmoisture laden and slow moving system. Also don't love seeing a \nsurface low near the area this time of year as it could enhance the \nlow level shear profile a bit. For now, will message shower and \nstorm chances through the weekend with highs in the mid 80s.",
